{"id":"05d6770f9ac38c68","group":"58","path":"58/batch04/58-df-crossing.md","title":"Crossing","display":"df-crossing — Crossing","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-crossing","aliases":["58-df-crossing"],"display":"df-crossing — Crossing","depends_on":["[[../batch05/58-df-knot.md]]","[[../batch14/58-df-transverse.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-crossing"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-crossing</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-crossing — Crossing"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ccaaf599ec318a33\" href=\"?note=ccaaf599ec318a33\" title=\"../batch05/58-df-knot.md\">../batch05/58-df-knot.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"f10cb4e88874efad\" href=\"?note=f10cb4e88874efad\" title=\"../batch14/58-df-transverse.md\">../batch14/58-df-transverse.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"D\\in V\">\\(D\\in V\\)</span> (knot or link diagram, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"ccaaf599ec318a33\" href=\"?note=ccaaf599ec318a33\" title=\"../batch05/58-df-knot.md\">../batch05/58-df-knot.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\pi\\in V\">\\(\\pi\\in V\\)</span> (diagram projection code)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p\\in\\mathbb R^2\">\\(p\\in\\mathbb R^2\\)</span> (double-point candidate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Crossing}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Crossing}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (crossing predicate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Transverse}_S\\subseteq V^4\">\\(\\operatorname{Transverse}_S\\subseteq V^4\\)</span> (transversality predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"f10cb4e88874efad\" href=\"?note=f10cb4e88874efad\" title=\"../batch14/58-df-transverse.md\">../batch14/58-df-transverse.md</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}crossing} \\vdash \\mathrm{Crossing}_S(p,D)\\leftrightarrow p\\in\\mathbb R^2\\land\\exists\\pi\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Function}(\\pi,D,\\mathbb R^2)\\land|\\pi^{-1}[\\{p\\}]|=2\\land\\operatorname{Transverse}_S(\\pi,\\{p\\},D,\\mathbb R^2)\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}crossing} \\vdash \\mathrm{Crossing}_S(p,D)\\leftrightarrow p\\in\\mathbb R^2\\land\\exists\\pi\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Function}(\\pi,D,\\mathbb R^2)\\land|\\pi^{-1}[\\{p\\}]|=2\\land\\operatorname{Transverse}_S(\\pi,\\{p\\},D,\\mathbb R^2)\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Crossings are transverse double points of planar diagrams.  The projection is now bound by the predicate, and transversality uses the four-argument upstream signature.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch05/58-df-knot.md","status":"resolved","id":"ccaaf599ec318a33","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch05/58-df-knot.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch14/58-df-transverse.md","status":"resolved","id":"f10cb4e88874efad","anchor":"r